    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d517">

                <pb facs="0946" n="886" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg886"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Hovey.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 97.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-10-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 3, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch of the 14th of September, No. 148. The President is gratified with the
                    prospect it gives of an acceptance of the tender of the good offices of this
                    government for the establishment of peace, between the allied republics of the
                    Pacific coast and Spain. The friendly sentiments expressed by the President of
                    Peru are appreciated.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvin P. Hovey</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">.&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
